Found under k261 (apply worker, 2026-10-31, by reading the code, not reproduced): an AMD GPU DaemonSet (device plugin, DRA driver, labeller, metrics exporter) changed outside OCP shows in ocp status / the dry run as drift a real run fixes (self_healing), but the AMD step compares only the recorded hash in .ocp/deployed.yaml and leaves the changed DaemonSet as it is. Related: the OCP::Drift POD calls those probes "report-only", while the code marks them self_healing.

First reproduce it (a test: a DaemonSet whose image or args differ from what OCP rendered, recorded hash unchanged). Then decide by what the step can know: compare the live object with what OCP would render (and redeploy), or mark the probe as report-only so status stops promising it. Done = status, dry run and the real run agree on that case (test), and the POD says what the code does.

2026-10-31 12:17 Reproduced (t/251, fakes; base HEAD 12d049a + k338 + k261, new test only): DaemonSet image set to 0.0.1, recorded hash unchanged. ocp status: 'AMD GPU device plugin runs rocm/k8s-device-plugin:0.0.1, expected rocm/k8s-device-plugin:1.31.0.11', counted fixable (self_healing). AMD step dry run: '[amd] AMD GPU device plugin is up to date on synapse', no change (the full dry run also prints the [drift] line and counts it as an action, so it contradicts itself). Real run: 'already deployed (up to date)' / '[ok] AMD GPU device plugin up to date', no deploy call, 0 changes, and the probe still finds the drift afterwards. Same for the labeller, the DRA driver and the metrics exporter. Red: t/251 2/41 subtests failed.

2026-10-31 12:17 Decision: (a), narrowed to what the probe reads. The step reads the DaemonSet as the k250 probe does (first container's image tag vs the pin, tag_prefix, leading v alike) through a shared OCP::Drift->version_against_pin and redeploys on a difference ('updated', 'ran X, expected Y'). Why not (b) report-only: a pin bump IS healed via the options hash, so report-only would make status wrong for the common case. Why not a full render: the full objects live in private Rex::Rancher _amd_*_specs, which OCP cannot see. Matches the k277 ClusterPolicy (compare only what OCP sets, re-apply on a difference) and ADR 0008 (hash never evidence alone, witness read). Args/other fields are neither reported by status nor healed by apply (tested), so the three agree there too. A refused image read = no verdict: the real run fails the component with the cause, the dry run says 'could not be checked' (k269).

